#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046645} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549095} :activity/id #uuid "edf24058-88a8-5581-b794-478468ae810a" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048878 :topic/id #uuid "c8e7edcb-eb86-52ac-9a3b-92e4b445b353" :topic/math-academy-id 3260} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549095 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549034 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ed2b512-fd94-527c-8aa7-14eb2e253d5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548448} {:answer/id #uuid "677c0d5e-9a4f-53b6-831c-38e8d4e4c8aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548550} {:answer/id #uuid "d42ea941-f8f4-516d-9716-11327749134c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548769} {:answer/id #uuid "ef82bee9-2b28-57a1-b630-a8d70ae2e61d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548829} {:answer/id #uuid "efa87d3d-378e-520b-80c5-c18393473402" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548830}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548829} :answer-field/id #uuid "d537a454-077e-5bec-8d5e-c804712b982d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548961}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "97f38e8d-e7da-59bd-ba74-56efb7ebb5d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-95741" :question/problem "$$\n\n$\\int \\operatorname{coth}⁡x(2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the trigonometry identity \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{coth}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{coth}⁡x(2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{csch}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "4a24ff8d-4408-5086-a362-5fda8f4d6863" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549107}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549100 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549045 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4094b1d6-e49d-5a4c-8130-b945454b28db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{65}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548478}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548478} :answer-field/id #uuid "25b5f170-7d01-575f-9c9a-1bf9fe7b0568" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ba7d332a-6786-594a-94f9-7b21daa8d15e" :question/math-academy-id "q-352941" :question/problem "$$\n\nEvaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}3\\operatorname{sech}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nFirst, we find the hyperbolic identities that correspond to the following trigonometric identities:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identities are\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x},\\,\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}3\\operatorname{sech}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\operatorname{sech}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3x)}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=3x.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=3x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡8$ |\n\nNow, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}3{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\operatorname{sech}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\operatorname{sech}⁡(u)\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(u)\\,\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sech}⁡(u){|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sech}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡8)+\\operatorname{sech}⁡(0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡8)}+1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(\\frac{8+{8}^{-1}}{2})}+1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(\\frac{65}{16})}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{49}{65}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "5732f6ba-37ef-5624-8851-8bc3a6396c11"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549107 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548976 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d5ae3f1-9426-5b71-9c8a-39ff341b203d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{240}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548469} {:answer/id #uuid "adaf5e80-f765-530e-bb4c-2a9cb2a2639f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{75}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548698} {:answer/id #uuid "e3b3d1f0-bf8f-570f-a904-dec2d7f66618" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{45}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548799} {:answer/id #uuid "efbf3afe-ee5e-5490-a69f-dee8cd1d6186" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{120}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548831} {:answer/id #uuid "f4838b2c-2ff8-52d4-bfdd-390ae6cc1518" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{110}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548841}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548469} :answer-field/id #uuid "fca0c653-f489-5a0b-b300-4fbf7f846779" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0266df41-acf0-5289-8790-ab60c8f211ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-96504" :question/problem "$$\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nFirst, recall the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csch}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{csch}^{2}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=2x.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=2x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡9$ |\n\nNow, we evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{csch}^{2}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}{csch}^{2}⁡u\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}{csch}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{coth}⁡u){|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡9)+\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}-1}+\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{{9}^{2}+1}{{9}^{2}-1}+\\frac{{4}^{2}+1}{{4}^{2}-1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{41}{40}+\\frac{17}{15}) \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{240}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7045c248-0444-5e93-afb7-d434ed35d42a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549123}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549121 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549013 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a0d7365-f518-5311-a5f3-c5f826b81b2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{e}^{4}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548467}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548467} :answer-field/id #uuid "40c090a2-44ae-5ef6-9984-cc694c4d8efa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "735acc88-33c3-52d8-953c-ec2e9e0254cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-346480" :question/problem "$$\n\nEvaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{{coth}^{2}⁡x}{2{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{{coth}^{2}⁡x}{2{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {coth}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow we need to find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the trigonometric identity \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{coth}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the above identity to write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {coth}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{csch}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡2-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡(1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{{e}^{2}+1}{{e}^{2}-1}-\\frac{{e}^{4}+1}{{e}^{4}-1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{({e}^{2}+1)^{2}-({e}^{4}+1)}{({e}^{4}-1)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{e}^{4}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "867e285f-fea0-51f6-8984-0117bc47c407" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549100}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549123 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167138 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9751268b-065e-530e-8f61-524e89ea5d81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x-2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548649} {:answer/id #uuid "c58bd0f4-783c-5d87-a549-3f629b85dc92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x-2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548746} {:answer/id #uuid "d5845fec-c7b4-59ef-afad-7f9f315af72e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548771} {:answer/id #uuid "efcfb69a-cb84-52fa-83e3-8c5deda2d628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x-2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548832} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f06524-c375-54b5-86ff-27ccebc4476b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{sinh}^{2}⁡x-2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548835}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548832} :answer-field/id #uuid "20dec17a-ebe7-549a-9b29-43f35de681f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163906}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "941a2692-f4e7-54c6-8e94-3c936c9ba118" :question/math-academy-id "q-165866" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\n$$\n\nFirst, we recall the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-2)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x-2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8ae138ac-bc59-5ae3-a741-0a8c4c2c3c10" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549121}}] :activity/title "Integration Using Basic Hyperbolic Identities" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548356}]}
